 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity**: $O(1)$. Constant number of arithmetic operations.
-- **Memory Complexity**: $O(1)$. No auxiliary data structures.
-- **Strengths**: Very fast evaluation. Variant A is extremely concise. Variant B is exact.
-- **Limitations**: Variant A is an approximation for the exact hexagonal shape (it effectively computes the distance to a specific linear approximation or a rotated hexagon). Variant B is more complex to implement correctly.
-- **When to use**: When a hexagonal cross-section is needed. Use Variant A for speed and simplicity if the orientation matches. Use Variant B for strict geometric accuracy.
